Evaluation 
 What Works Well
•	Keyboard navigation works on major interactive elements (tab key traverses’ input, filters, and sort dropdown).
•	Sufficient colour contrast between background and text.
•	Clear text labels on search, filters, and buttons.

Identified WCAG Compliance Issues
Issue	WCAG Reference	Description
Missing ARIA roles and labels	1.3.1 Info and Relationships
Elements like dropdowns and cards lack ARIA roles and labels.
No visible focus indication	2.4.7 Focus Visible
Tabbing through elements does not always show visible focus.
Non-descriptive link/button text	2.4.4 Link Purpose (In Context)
Example: “Click” or “Play” buttons don’t describe what video they affect.
No skip-to-content link	2.4.1 Bypass Blocks
Users cannot skip navigation to reach main content directly.
Image alt text missing	1.1.1 Non-text Content
Video thumbnails lack alt text for screen readers.



Recommendations for Improving Accessibility
1.	Add ARIA roles and landmarks
Use roles like role="main", role="navigation", and ARIA attributes for dropdowns.
2.	Ensure focus is visible
Use: focus styles in CSS to highlight focused elements clearly.
3.	Provide descriptive text for buttons
Instead of generic “Play” or “Click,” use “Play Advanced React video” etc.
4.	Add alt attributes to all images
Example: <img src="..." alt="Thumbnail for React Basics" />
5.	Include a “Skip to Main Content” link
Especially useful for keyboard and screen reader users.
6.	Validate with Lighthouse or axe-core
Use automated accessibility tools to catch more issues

